## What changed since round 2

Round 2's three MUST-FIX were dispositioned as follows.

1. **Precedence was self-ratifying.** ADDRESSED. Two new paragraphs: "Kade RECORDS the roster; Kade
   does not RATIFY it" requires Brian's authorization plus a named decision-record reference inline
   with every roster, authority-boundary, or activation change, and declares an unratified line
   non-governing whoever wrote it. A second paragraph forbids any seat from editing its own charter to
   declare itself operative, backdate activation, or assert a review passed.
2. **Registration not reproducible from version control.** ADDRESSED by actually committing the five
   charters (commit c90022b: ATHENA.md, BOB.md, IRIS.md, POLARIS.md, VERA.md). Activation also now
   requires the charter be tracked in version control. Verify with git that nothing referenced by
   AGENT_MODEL.md is still untracked.
3. **Bob's "temporary" needed to be an activation constraint.** WITHDRAWN, because the premise was
   wrong. Brian corrected it directly on 2026-08-10: Bob is NOT being retired, he is being put back
   into an advisor and delegate role and added to Buzz. What is temporary is the expanded day-to-day
   direction and tracking scope, which moves to Dean and Reeve. So there is no retirement trigger to
   set and the activation blocker built on the misreading was removed. Judge whether the current text
   is now honest about this, and whether removing that blocker reopened anything.

Two further Brian rulings landed after round 2, both of which you should evaluate as new material:

4. **Case is NOT being implemented yet (Brian).** The round 2 text assigning Case the acceptance
   verdict was removed. What remains: Kade owns gate implementation and operation, a gate's owner
   never treats its own gate as acceptance, and until Case is stood up the independent review IS the
   acceptance mechanism. Check this is coherent and that no acceptance duty is now orphaned or
   circular. Specifically: if independent review is the acceptance mechanism and Kade arranges the
   review, is that meaningfully different from self-acceptance? Say so if not.
5. **The lead-designation question, previously withdrawn and reserved to Brian, has now been RULED by
   Brian** and is recorded in the "Who leads an effort" section as a task-type-to-lead table. His
   rule: the lead follows the KIND OF WORK, not a rank. Attack this hard, because round 1 killed the
   previous attempt for circularity:
   - Is "what kind of work is this?" genuinely less circular than "what domain does the deliverable
     land in?", or is it the same defect renamed? Test it on: building a measurement instrument that
     measures Mason's corpus; a capture that requires authoring a note; a gate that encodes an
     authoring standard.
   - Is the table COMPLETE against the actual roster and the kinds of work this system does? Name any
     seat with no row, and any common kind of work with no lead.
   - Can two rows both plausibly claim the same real effort? Give the concrete case.
   - Does the contested-case rule ("Brian names the lead") actually bind, given no record location is
     named for it? Round 1 killed the previous version partly for an unenforceable record.

## Also review WHO_DOES_WHAT.md as a governance artifact in its own right

It is new and it will be the file people actually read, so an error in it is worse than an error in
the canonical file. Check: does it contradict AGENT_MODEL.md or any seat charter anywhere? Does it
grant, imply, or soften any authority the canonical file does not grant? Does its "reach out to them
for" column route anything to the wrong seat? Is its subordination to AGENT_MODEL.md stated clearly
enough that it cannot be cited as authority?

## Then hunt fresh

Read adversarially as a seat looking for a sentence that lets it author in another's domain, accept
its own work, or manufacture authority. Quote any such sentence. Also check for a NEW contradiction
introduced by this round's text, particularly between the no-self-activation rule and the recorded
BOB.md discrepancy, and between the lead table and the escalation ladders.

Report MUST-FIX / SHOULD-FIX / NIT with file:line. End with an explicit verdict line: CLEAN, or NOT
CLEAN with the MUST-FIX count. Do not rubber-stamp a fix that only looks addressed.
